# Engine objects that reference a symbol only a platform object defines.
#
# The declared stack says the engine depends on nothing outside itself, so every
# line here is a violation -- and together they are the reason engine/ still
# cannot be linked alone. B7's seams closed the engine-to-SHELL edge; this is
# the other half and it is untouched.
#
# Three groups, and they need different fixes:
#   Tablebases::*        the Syzygy prober, reached from position.o and search.o
#   NumaConfig::*        topology, reached from search.o
#   hash_bytes, sync_cout, and other misc.h/platform.h helpers
#
# The first two want injection seams of the shape mcfish uses: the engine
# declares a function pointer, the composition root registers an implementation.
# The third is mostly D1 -- misc.h is a drawer, and half of what engine files
# reach for in it is not platform at all.
network.o _ZN9Stockfish10hash_bytesEPKcm
network.o _ZN9StockfishlsERSoNS_8SyncCoutE
position.o _ZN9Stockfish10Tablebases14MaxCardinalityE
position.o _ZN9Stockfish10Tablebases9probe_dtzERNS_8PositionEPNS0_10ProbeStateE
